{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-jacobson}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f582284e5f87930f321b0d79512743027b4c24b27ff395a1259f5e9659a5d4c6", "source_text": "Jacobson schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a71542e9ce79c250c7fc0d89fc87ca558153527d40265beba85e6d74bab4e4fb", "unit_id": "tag:01P1:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-space-jacobson}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4fb1b01357791f8065d2ac918bda2d66a4551486c26abda226d4ade480b28122", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a space is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Jacobson<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the closed points are\ndense in every closed subset, see\nTopology, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:35697f9605b61050b5bade150f8caa910d94e664c95d6fbed84b34ffe59cd836", "unit_id": "tag:01P1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-jacobson}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86ec2eecd570d0c8a4f479624baf284069e51967c1f2fc353abd21054aea9915", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:979f88eef623942a7d507763162f32f692ac3c461d8b199a4bd03c18dbe372ec", "source_text": "A scheme <MATH_0001> is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Jacobson<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if its underlying topological\nspace is Jacobson.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3cebb784c9c4db59e76845ab00b48367843cd01ba0295874cbfd5e15f7f5a2d7", "unit_id": "tag:01P2:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-ring-jacobson}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:103c4d2b7eba8315df9a978e976ac0b41d8778b6af7fbee40f280209877d12d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6cfcdf6dc520e10fa69ddbc40346754d48b33576d9257e656ad718ebf325fde1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring <MATH_0001> is Jacobson if every radical ideal of <MATH_0002>\nis the intersection of maximal ideals, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fd0e91385d56fdf53781d46c322fbe15233ce20d75ecd3ca126f3dc05aa4d6f9", "unit_id": "tag:01P1:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0002": "$R$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-jacobson}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72f2b0124eafdd1da09167458b55c534aba1cfa49c955d32132784a32416dd19", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4fab0e238659a48c26a82141e5f4469712d1272e93aeed5d1123477dfc735b5", "source_text": "An affine scheme <MATH_0001> is Jacobson if and only if\nthe ring <MATH_0002> is Jacobson.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bcbd84e799771af1de871b56315e8fed6c927382e7f05a6cae1a527c401a527e", "unit_id": "tag:01P3:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-jacobson}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1998ac87913ca04c65dda3eeca5e6128670380e0122933d7ff959a586184acb", "source_text": "This is Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57dca754073f5a90b03cc831903eb92e5583ff863f4283145a771a9ab8ad8d51", "unit_id": "tag:01P3:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8188165cdb7a098951be4cae1b383af45827bf0caae7bdb0175e890b169bf57a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00526ab52bccfefde57d9d5f8fc9b76a7e1c01b8474b13c93b6368ef3ff4c69c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the standard result characterizing Jacobson schemes.\nIntuitively it claims that Jacobson <MATH_0001> locally Jacobson.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4661a093a39fedf13d6da2fd38b6ae40a909955cbbaae2edd69c584884b123b8", "unit_id": "tag:01P1:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0006": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0008": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X_j$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-locally-P}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-jacobson}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cbf58c2b6bbfd7f2d6bbf6c0904d22a85902a4d79a65c4bd806e5562a6fdb21c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c156cfbc40be71c8ff21556b8634082826aa5df5be5ed52ce7bc593088e6b0b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is Jacobson.\n<STRUCT_0003> The scheme <MATH_0003> is ``locally Jacobson'' in the sense of\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0004> For every affine open <MATH_0004> the ring <MATH_0005>\nis Jacobson.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0006> such that\neach <MATH_0007> is Jacobson.\n<STRUCT_0006> There exists an open covering <MATH_0008>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0009> is Jacobson.\n<STRUCT_0007>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0010> is Jacobson then every open subscheme\nis Jacobson.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d90327713c2d7941b5f7949c4a8fdb161c12896561339d6217715e1411f88c3a", "unit_id": "tag:01P4:statement"}
